Z||000000||mrgone||10-23-2001||05:45 PM||||i have a few questions and wonderings about clutches<BR>first heres a background on what i know and have experienced on my car<P>until last night when the clutch died, ive always had to push the clutch to the floor when shifting gears, it wouldnt shift with it pushed halfway. the clutch was obviousley very worn and easy to learn how to drive stick on.<P>ive heard mixed responces from people about shifting with the clutch 1/2 in. my roomates cavilier.<P>also, im a bit concerned when i get the car back. (they are replacing a clutch cylinder first) I havent driven any other car thats manual tranny other than mine, so.. what should i expect? will it be super tight and prone to me stalling it? (ive only stalled the car a handful of times ever)<P>sorry of my ignorance, im going to check out the 'how things work' webpage and see if clutches are on there before i check my replies. i have an idea but i want to know for sure.<P>thanks.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-23-2001||05:57 PM||||All cars are different, but you should like yours with a new clutch.  It should have a nice positive feel to it.<P>If you want to see the technical end of it, go to a good news stand.  The current issue of Practical Classics (English) has a good description of the different types of clutches and how they work.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
